ase 9: UI/UX & HCI Design Polish
This phase transforms the functional POS system into a premium, state-of-the-art application. We will focus on modern aesthetics, consistent design patterns, and enhanced Human-Computer Interaction (HCI) principles.

User Review Required
IMPORTANT

Design Direction: I am proposing a "Modern Dark/Glassmorphic" theme by default, as it feels high-end and reduces eye strain for long-shift cashiers. Would you prefer a Clean Light Mode, a Sleek Dark Mode, or a toggle for both?

Iconography: I will use Lucide-React icons for the interface. This will require a quick npm install lucide-react. Do you approve adding this dependency?

Proposed Changes
1. The Foundation (CSS Design System)
[MODIFY] client/src/assets/css/styles.css
Complete overhaul of the CSS variables.
Implementation of a "Glassmorphism" utility set.
Definition of a premium typography scale using 'Inter' or 'Outfit'.
Addition of micro-animation classes (hover-scale, fade-in, slide-up).
2. Global Architecture (HCI: Consistency & Standards)
[NEW] client/src/components/MainLayout.jsx
A reusable wrapper for all authenticated pages.
Sidebar: Persistent navigation with high-visibility active states.
Topbar: User status, notifications, and clear logout access.
[MODIFY] client/src/App.jsx
Wrap protected routes in the new MainLayout.
3. Visual Overhaul (Aesthetics & Premium Feel)
[MODIFY] client/src/pages/LoginPage.jsx
Create a "Wowed" first impression with a dynamic background and a glassmorphic login card.
Add input focus effects and improved error states.
[MODIFY] client/src/pages/SalesPage.jsx
HCI: Efficiency of Use: Optimize the terminal layout. Larger touch targets, clearer pricing hierarchy.
Smooth transitions when items enter/exit the cart.
[MODIFY] Pages: Products, Inventory, Customers, Reports
Transition from plain tables to Modern Data Cards or Refined Data Grids.
Use meaningful colors (e.g., semantic greens for sales, soft reds for low stock).
4. Interactive Feedback (HCI: System Status)
Implementation of a global Toast Notification system for better "Visibility of System Status."
Loading skeletons for data-heavy sections (Reports/Inventory).
Verification Plan
Automated Verification
Lighthouse Audit: Check for performance, accessibility, and best practices.
Browser Testing: Verify glassmorphic effects and animations across Chrome/Edge.
Manual Verification
Verify that every "Add/Delete/Edit" action provides clear visual feedback (Toasts).
Ensure the "Low Stock" warning is visually prominent but not distracting (HCI: Error Prevention).
Check responsiveness on "Tablet" view (common for POS hardware).
